  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The cost of specialisation",
      "items": [
        "Each role is a separate agent with its own prompt, model choice, and failure mode",
        "Shared state is the only coordination channel — a stale read is the most common multi-agent bug"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "When this is a mistake",
      "items": [
        "If the reviewer almost always approves, the split is paying for coordination it does not use",
        "Start single-agent; add roles only when a demonstrated need resists a better prompt"
      ]
